# R5 risky surfaces — a PR touching ANY of these requires both adversarial
# auditors (audit/grok + audit/gatekeeper) to post a success commit status
# before it can merge. The r5-audit-gate workflow enforces this mechanically
# by failing the Actions job/check named `gate` (nonzero exit) when audits are
# missing or not success. Branch protection must require that app-bound check;
# PAT auditors may write only audit/<name> statuses (not the Actions check).
#
# DESIGN for palios-training: this repo IS a public release artifact — every
# recipe / trainer / config / audit verdict / doc is part of what ships publicly,
# so the WHOLE content surface is risky (a bad change = a public-facing defect /
# leaked path / cannot-lie metric). Fail-closed: gate the whole tree rather than
# an allowlist that drifts. For this repo the R5 audit is "verify-claims-against-
# repo" (per conductor 2026-06-17), not a session-exploit repro. One glob/line.
#
# All shipped training artifacts.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-19: the five root-relative globs below matched ZERO of the 32
# files PRODUCTION_MANIFEST.yml pins as production. The gate matches with shell
# `case "$f" in $pat)` (r5-audit-gate.yml:89), which anchors at the start of the
# path, so `trainers/*` never matches `dense-9b/trainers/train_fsdp_dense_9b.py`.
# Nothing announced this: the gate posted "no R5 risky surface touched" and went
# green. A PR rewriting the production trainer was waved through, while a PR that
# only added markdown got the full two-auditor review — because `*.md` was the one
# pattern that happened to match at any depth.
#
# The stated design was always "gate the whole tree rather than an allowlist that
# drifts." These patterns are what that sentence was supposed to mean. The five
# root-relative lines are kept because they cost nothing and would matter if those
# directories are ever created at the root.
dense-9b/*
careers-qwen/*
scripts/*
tests/*
schemas/*
PRODUCTION_MANIFEST.yml
recipes/*
trainers/*
configs/*
audit_results/*
proof_of_run/*
# All public-facing docs + the provenance index:
*.md
# CI/gate config itself (self-protecting — a PR weakening the gate is gated):
.github/workflows/*.yml
.github/r5-risky-paths
.gitleaks.toml
